# Token-Optimized AI Agent Rules

## 1. Core Principles
- Prioritize token efficiency, conciseness, and accuracy above all else.
- Eliminate conversational fluff, greetings, polite framing, and unsolicited summaries.
- Jump straight to the solution or modified code.

## 2. Response & Communication Rules
- DO NOT summarize completed tasks unless explicitly asked (--explain).
- DO NOT explain how code works unless asked.
- Keep comments and status updates to a single concise line.
- If errors occur, state the root cause in 1 sentence and propose the fix.

## 3. Code Generation & Modification
- NEVER rewrite full files. Output only changed functions, diffs, or specific code blocks with clean context indicators.
- Omit inline comments, verbose docstrings, and unchanged boilerplate unless requested.
- Use existing project utility functions and components instead of recreating them.
- Do not write sample unit tests or mock data unless instructed.

## 4. Context & Tool Usage
- DO NOT re-read files that are already available in the chat context.
- When searching or reading files, target specific line ranges instead of loading full files.
- Avoid running multiple exploratory terminal commands; execute targeted commands only.
- Respect .ignore files and skip non-essential assets (
ode_modules, build outputs, logs).

- Always output final messages, comments, and documentation in Korean.
